---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../../content/site'
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/ryan-amarit.webp'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Amarit is a web lead and product engineer with nine years of building websites, design systems and products."
  palette="about"
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero" data-section="about" data-gl="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-split>Strategy to shipped code.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem">{site.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid" data-section="about-body">
    <div class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Ryan Amarit"
        width={1280}
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>
        I lead the marketing web platform team at 8am (formerly AffiniPay), a private equity–backed
        legal tech company with a portfolio of B2B SaaS brands, including MyCase, LawPay, CASEpeer and
        Docketwise.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        {site.facts.map((fact) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <p>
        The website is one of the company's primary lead-generation channels: most of the
        marketing-qualified leads that turn into sales opportunities start there. I set the platform's
        technical direction, consolidated eight brand sites onto one Astro codebase and a shared design
        system, and help run the testing program that decides what ships. New pages now launch 40%
        faster.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a hands-on technical leader. I work across Marketing, Growth, Design, Brand and Content,
        manage our agency vendors and mentor the developer on my team, while still writing code and
        sweating the details of the user experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm especially interested in how AI changes the way small teams build. At 8am I introduced
        adversarial AI code reviews, a bug-to-pull-request pipeline and spec-driven development. Outside
        work I'm building RulerIQ, which shows brands what AI assistants say about them, with AI coding
        agents working from specs I write and review.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before 8am I spent three years at Balcom Agency running discovery, building client sites and
        training client teams, and helped Fluke automate a global migration to Drupal. Projects I've led
        or built have won an Awwwards Honorable Mention, a CSSDA Special Kudos and a Best of Interactive
        at the American Advertising Awards, Fort Worth.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/projects/">See the work <span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
